From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 06:29:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] setup: recognize current-generation manylinux images

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted; generalizes a check that predates manylinux_2_28+]

is_manylinux() only recognizes manylinux1/manylinux2010/manylinux2014 by
matching three hardcoded /etc/redhat-release strings (CentOS 5.11/6.10/
7.9.2009). quay.io/pypa/manylinux_2_39_riscv64 (this repo's riscv64 image,
PEP 600) is Rocky Linux 10-based and matches none of them, so
is_manylinux() silently returns False inside it. That flag drives two
decisions in my_cmake_build.run(): the CMake build type (Release vs.
RelWithDebInfo, the latter keeping full debug info -- "too large for
wheels" per this same file's own comment) and the default STDCXX (17 vs.
20), plus my_install.run()'s cxxversion-advertising rewrite ("reset the
default cxxversion to 20 if no user override" on real manylinux builds).
Misdetecting manylinux here would ship a riscv64 wheel built differently
(bigger, debug-laden, and advertising a C++ standard it wasn't actually
built with) from every other published platform.

All pypa/manylinux images, including the newer PEP 600 (_2_28/_2_34/
_2_39) generations, bake in AUDITWHEEL_PLAT (the policy auditwheel itself
targets, e.g. manylinux_2_39_riscv64) -- a stable, generation-independent
marker. Check it first and keep the existing string match as a fallback
for the images it already recognized.

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 cling/setup.py | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/cling/setup.py b/cling/setup.py
index d7826bf..8dbdf4e 100755
--- a/cling/setup.py
+++ b/cling/setup.py
@@ -44,6 +44,11 @@ def is_manylinux():
     global _is_manylinux
     if _is_manylinux is None:
         _is_manylinux = False
+        # all pypa/manylinux images, including the PEP 600 generations that
+        # post-date the CentOS-release checks below, export this.
+        if os.environ.get('AUDITWHEEL_PLAT', '').startswith('manylinux'):
+            _is_manylinux = True
+            return _is_manylinux
         try:
             for line in open('/etc/redhat-release').readlines():
               # mark manylinux1, manylinux2010, or manylinux2014
